WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.452
Exercise 4: design contract-first.

2
00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:09.451
The purchasing team wants SKU sales per year. You build the data product.

3
00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:15.139
Create the new contract and open it in the editor.

4
00:00:15.189 --> 00:00:21.834
Contract first: design the interface before writing any SQL.

5
00:00:21.884 --> 00:00:35.220
The server: the analytics schema, where the view will live.

6
00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:43.769
The schema: a view called sku_sales_per_year.

7
00:00:43.819 --> 00:01:07.801
Four properties: sku and year are dimensions for grouping.

8
00:01:07.851 --> 00:01:40.385
order_count and total_quantity are measures, with their aggregation as transformLogic.

9
00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:51.486
Context tells AI agents how to query the product correctly.

10
00:01:51.536 --> 00:01:56.015
Save. The contract is the specification for the implementation.

11
00:01:56.065 --> 00:02:05.102
Run the tests: red. The view does not exist yet, and that is the point.

12
00:02:05.152 --> 00:02:21.560
The data product: consumerAligned, with an input port on orders_v2.

13
00:02:21.611 --> 00:02:28.861
Valid ODPS 1.1. Consumers can review the interface now. Next: implement it.
